{
  // Tool descriptions for tcp-mcp-tasks. Each tool is mode-gated — call the
  // one matching your assignment's mode. Call describe_server first for details.
  "describe_server": "Returns an overview of the tasks service and the tool you must use to complete your assignment, tailored to your current mode.",
  "create_plan": "PLAN MODE ONLY. Submits the plan for your task: an ordered list of assignments, each with a prompt, a role to carry it out, its expected outputs, and optional materials. You MUST call this as your final action — a narrated plan is not accepted. Call describe_server first for the exact shape of each assignment.",
  "complete_assignment": "IMPLEMENT, FINALISE OR CONSULTEE MODE. Submits your finished assignment: a concise summary plus the artifacts you prepared, each `{ type, value }` with type `file` (a filename in your working directory) or `text` (literal text). Resource drafts you wrote with write_resource are found automatically. Your prepared artifacts must satisfy the assignment's expected outputs — files are verified to exist. You MUST call this as your final action after the work is done.",
  "assure_assignment": "QA MODE ONLY. Records your QA verdict on the assignment under review: qa must be exactly `accept` or `reject` (case-insensitive) — reject requires actionable feedback for the implementing agent. You MUST call this as your final action.",
  "fail_assignment": "Ends your assignment as failed, when it can't be done. Use it only after trying other approaches and, where you can, asking a user with request_user_input. reason: `data_protection` (it would mean storing data on the company's do-not-store list), `tools_exhausted` (you tried every approach and the tools still fail), or `information_unavailable` (information the task needs can't be found or obtained). explanation: one or two sentences the user will read."
}
